# `random-item` is committed here on purpose, and the repository root ignores every
# directory called `node_modules`, so this file un-ignores exactly this one. The long form
# of the reasoning is in `../wrap-ansi/.gitignore`; the short form is that slice-ansi's own
# suite opens with `import randomItem from 'random-item'`, a vendored suite is run unedited,
# and without it the control run fails to *resolve* rather than failing a case:
#
#     Error [ERR_MODULE_NOT_FOUND]: Cannot find package 'random-item' imported from
#     packages/compat-oracle/vendor/slice-ansi/test.js
#
# `random-item` has no dependencies of its own, so this is one directory and five files.
#
# The same hazard applies: `npm run compat -- --vendor` deletes `vendor/slice-ansi/` whole
# before re-copying. Restore with `git checkout -- packages/compat-oracle/vendor/slice-ansi/node_modules`.
!node_modules/

# ava's per-run scratch file — a record of which cases failed on this machine last time.
node_modules/.cache/
